1
00:01:28,284 --> 00:01:34,123
NINJA VS. INDIANA RYOTSU

2
00:01:35,758 --> 00:01:36,659
Good morning.

3
00:01:36,892 --> 00:01:37,926
Good morning, sir.

4
00:01:38,127 --> 00:01:39,628
Hi, good morning.

5
00:01:39,828 --> 00:01:40,696
Hmm?

6
00:01:41,063 --> 00:01:43,165
Ryotsu, what's with that outfit?

7
00:01:44,466 --> 00:01:47,903
Oh, well... I'm just going out on patrol.

8
00:01:48,637 --> 00:01:51,373
When did you join the mountain patrol, huh?

9
00:01:51,907 --> 00:01:53,809
Well, it's dangerous out there these days.

10
00:01:54,009 --> 00:01:57,146
We need equipment like this to patrol properly.

11
00:01:57,346 --> 00:01:58,380
Stop making excuses!

12
00:01:59,014 --> 00:02:01,917
He won't explain, no matter how much we ask.

13
00:02:03,719 --> 00:02:05,254
Ryo-san, are you ready?

14
00:02:05,921 --> 00:02:07,356
It's about time to—

15
00:02:07,556 --> 00:02:09,291
Oh, directions to the station?

16
00:02:09,491 --> 00:02:11,460
Go straight this way and...

17
00:02:11,660 --> 00:02:14,530
Sorry, go ahead without me. I'll catch up soon.

18
00:02:14,730 --> 00:02:16,932
Ryotsu, what's going on?

19
00:02:17,166 --> 00:02:18,167
Huh?

20
00:02:18,367 --> 00:02:21,036
Wasn't that Shuzaburo Himeji?

21
00:02:21,270 --> 00:02:24,540
Shuzaburo Himeji, the famous archaeologist?

22
00:02:24,973 --> 00:02:28,177
I heard last year he dug up Mount Akagi with a bulldozer

23
00:02:28,377 --> 00:02:30,679
to try to unearth Tokugawa's buried treasure.

24
00:02:31,113 --> 00:02:32,815
He didn't find anything, though.

25
00:02:33,015 --> 00:02:35,984
Well, I guess I'll head out on patrol.

26
00:02:36,885 --> 00:02:41,223
Ryo-chan, don't tell me you're going after buried treasure with that guy?

27
00:02:42,057 --> 00:02:43,559
Buried treasure?

28
00:02:43,759 --> 00:02:47,162
Are you planning something stupid again?

29
00:02:47,363 --> 00:02:49,398
It's rude to call it stupid.

30
00:02:49,598 --> 00:02:53,202
You should call it what it is. A man's dream!

31
00:02:53,402 --> 00:02:55,404
A man's dream, huh?

32
00:02:56,004 --> 00:02:59,742
The best thing for a man is to work steadily and live steadily.

33
00:02:59,975 --> 00:03:04,913
It's not manly to go looking for buried treasure to try to get rich quick.

34
00:03:05,381 --> 00:03:09,251
Ryotsu, it's not that easy to find buried treasure.

35
00:03:10,419 --> 00:03:11,687
Well, just wait and see.

36
00:03:11,887 --> 00:03:14,423
Right, I'll leave you guys to take care of things here.

37
00:03:14,790 --> 00:03:16,258
Hey, wait, Ryotsu!

38
00:03:17,860 --> 00:03:22,765
Jeez, that guy will do anything that leads to money.

39
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:26,001
But does it really exist?

40
00:03:26,735 --> 00:03:29,872
Is there really a castle that no one has found yet?

41
00:03:30,072 --> 00:03:32,007
We have to believe the ancient book.

42
00:03:33,342 --> 00:03:34,176
Hello!

43
00:03:34,476 --> 00:03:35,944
Oh, hello!

44
00:03:36,178 --> 00:03:37,646
Yeah, thank you.

45
00:03:38,080 --> 00:03:40,382
Look, there are so many hikers.

46
00:03:41,016 --> 00:03:42,951
That's why it's called a phantom castle.

47
00:03:43,185 --> 00:03:45,754
"There stands a hidden castle deep in the Kai mountains

48
00:03:45,954 --> 00:03:48,357
It's called the Phantom Castle.

49
00:03:48,557 --> 00:03:53,128
At its peak are a pair of &lt;i&gt;shachihoko&lt;/i&gt; with shimmering golden scales."

50
00:03:53,662 --> 00:03:55,831
Real orcas don't have any scales.

51
00:03:56,064 --> 00:04:00,836
But &lt;i&gt;shachihoko&lt;/i&gt; are imaginary sea creatures, modeled after orcas.

52
00:04:01,603 --> 00:04:05,407
Placing one at each end of a roof is said to protect the building from fire.

53
00:04:05,607 --> 00:04:07,609
I don't care about all that crap,

54
00:04:07,976 --> 00:04:11,380
but are those &lt;i&gt;shachihoko&lt;/i&gt; really made of solid gold?

55
00:04:11,580 --> 00:04:14,817
Yes, because Kai had gold mines.

56
00:04:15,050 --> 00:04:17,386
They were made by melting many large gold coins.

57
00:04:17,653 --> 00:04:19,988
I'm not really interested in their value,

58
00:04:20,222 --> 00:04:23,292
but from their size, the pair must be worth at least a billion.

59
00:04:23,992 --> 00:04:26,662
W-What? A billion yen?!

60
00:04:26,862 --> 00:04:28,230
Tell me that first!

61
00:04:28,430 --> 00:04:30,799
In that case, we've got no time to lose!

62
00:04:30,999 --> 00:04:33,402
Let's hurry up and find the castle.

63
00:04:33,602 --> 00:04:37,639
I just want to find Takeda Shingen's hidden castle...

64
00:04:39,441 --> 00:04:41,143
"KOFU"

65
00:04:41,443 --> 00:04:44,546
This road isn't on the navigation system. Which way is it?

66
00:04:44,780 --> 00:04:45,614
This way.

67
00:04:49,985 --> 00:04:51,987
Are you sure this is the right path?

68
00:04:52,187 --> 00:04:54,523
I'm sure! It's just as the ancient book says.

69
00:04:55,657 --> 00:04:56,792
Huh?

70
00:04:57,860 --> 00:04:59,628
What on earth is this?

71
00:05:00,495 --> 00:05:02,698
Hmm... well...

72
00:05:02,898 --> 00:05:05,000
This looks like Shingen's hidden hot spring.

73
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:09,705
Hey, we're not looking for a hot spring resort!

74
00:05:09,905 --> 00:05:10,873
Huh?

75
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:12,674
What?

76
00:05:13,442 --> 00:05:16,845
You're not talking about that &lt;i&gt;shachihoko&lt;/i&gt;, are you?

77
00:05:17,045 --> 00:05:18,180
No, no!

78
00:05:19,281 --> 00:05:22,985
That's strange. There's no hot spring on the map.

79
00:05:23,185 --> 00:05:26,488
Jeez, I've got a bad feeling about this.

80
00:05:26,688 --> 00:05:29,825
Oh! Look, there's a path.

81
00:05:30,492 --> 00:05:33,295
I knew the ancient book would lead us the right way.

82
00:05:38,367 --> 00:05:40,602
This is a dead end, seriously.

83
00:05:41,169 --> 00:05:43,338
That ancient book is a joke.

84
00:05:43,906 --> 00:05:44,740
Hmm...

85
00:05:45,374 --> 00:05:49,545
Well, maybe it's supposed to be this way up or...

86
00:05:49,745 --> 00:05:51,313
Hey, let me take a look!

87
00:05:51,513 --> 00:05:53,382
Stop that! What are you doing?

88
00:05:53,582 --> 00:05:56,585
This is a valuable book I found through great effort.

89
00:05:56,785 --> 00:05:58,954
-Just give it to me! -No!

90
00:05:59,187 --> 00:06:00,589
-Hand it over! -No!

91
00:06:07,162 --> 00:06:08,096
I'm dizzy!

92
00:06:13,268 --> 00:06:14,703
Ouch...

93
00:06:15,203 --> 00:06:17,339
Hey, are you okay?

94
00:06:17,539 --> 00:06:19,708
Yeah, I think so.

95
00:06:19,908 --> 00:06:23,111
But it looks like we fell down quite a long way.

96
00:06:25,213 --> 00:06:27,883
Thanks to that, we saved a lot of time.

97
00:06:28,083 --> 00:06:29,418
Don't talk crap!

98
00:06:29,618 --> 00:06:32,454
-Oh, there's a house over there. -Huh?

99
00:06:32,955 --> 00:06:34,957
It looks like a teahouse.

100
00:06:35,457 --> 00:06:37,759
Hey, we're gonna take a break here!

101
00:06:38,961 --> 00:06:40,228
I'm coming.

102
00:06:41,797 --> 00:06:43,999
Welcome.

103
00:06:44,232 --> 00:06:46,234
-We'll have some tea and dumplings. -Sure.

104
00:06:48,937 --> 00:06:51,473
Where are you guys going?

105
00:06:52,074 --> 00:06:55,644
Oh, actually we're looking for something around here.

106
00:06:57,245 --> 00:07:01,483
Oh, what kind of thing are you looking for?

107
00:07:01,683 --> 00:07:05,988
Well, we were just walking in the mountains and got a little lost.

108
00:07:06,822 --> 00:07:08,790
-Right? -Oh, yes, yes.

109
00:07:08,991 --> 00:07:11,293
-But you know... -Yes?

110
00:07:12,627 --> 00:07:15,964
You can't get many customers in a place like this.

111
00:07:16,465 --> 00:07:21,637
Oh, sometimes there are customers who wander in like you guys.

112
00:07:22,004 --> 00:07:25,173
-No need to worry. -Oh, I see.

113
00:07:28,443 --> 00:07:31,647
Well, after finishing your dumplings, you can go down that way.

114
00:07:31,847 --> 00:07:34,983
Walk a little further, and you'll reach the mountain trail.

115
00:07:37,953 --> 00:07:39,321
What should we do, Ryo-san?

116
00:07:40,155 --> 00:07:42,858
My gut tells me it's definitely this way.

117
00:07:43,058 --> 00:07:45,460
I can smell gold ahead.

118
00:07:45,661 --> 00:07:48,630
-Sorry, I just farted. -Gah...

119
00:07:50,499 --> 00:07:53,268
Old man, I'll leave the money here.

120
00:07:53,735 --> 00:07:56,304
-You can keep the change. -Wait a minute!

121
00:07:56,505 --> 00:07:57,305
What?

122
00:07:58,974 --> 00:08:01,276
What do you mean by this thousand yen?

123
00:08:01,476 --> 00:08:03,545
What is it? Too much?

124
00:08:04,646 --> 00:08:05,981
Don't be ridiculous!

125
00:08:06,748 --> 00:08:09,851
A cup of tea is 500 yen, three dumplings are 1,000 yen,

126
00:08:10,052 --> 00:08:11,920
so the total for both of you is 3,000 yen.

127
00:08:12,154 --> 00:08:14,056
Now pay up, every last yen!

128
00:08:14,389 --> 00:08:16,558
Th-Three thousand yen?

129
00:08:16,758 --> 00:08:17,926
Damn it!

130
00:08:18,160 --> 00:08:20,629
You old scoundrel, taking advantage of your customers!

131
00:08:20,829 --> 00:08:24,733
There's no electricity, gas, or running water in the mountains.

132
00:08:24,933 --> 00:08:27,202
Even 3,000 yen hardly covers the cost.

133
00:08:27,402 --> 00:08:29,204
Okay, I get it. I'll pay.

134
00:08:29,404 --> 00:08:31,106
Ryo-san, let's hurry anyway.

135
00:08:31,339 --> 00:08:33,575
Yeah, here you go!

136
00:08:35,210 --> 00:08:38,580
Well, well, thank you very much. Please come again.

137
00:08:39,214 --> 00:08:40,749
I'll never come again!

138
00:08:41,249 --> 00:08:43,085
No, no! Not that way!

139
00:08:43,919 --> 00:08:46,221
I told you the mountain trail is the other way.

140
00:08:46,421 --> 00:08:48,023
This way leads to a dead end.

141
00:08:48,223 --> 00:08:50,492
And if you go without permission, you'll be cursed!

142
00:08:50,692 --> 00:08:52,094
Cursed?

143
00:08:52,327 --> 00:08:55,130
Hah! Nonsense. Now move aside.

144
00:09:04,606 --> 00:09:07,976
Oh, it really was a dead end.

145
00:09:08,877 --> 00:09:12,380
Jeez, it's just like that rip-off teahouse owner said.

146
00:09:12,748 --> 00:09:17,886
-But I'm sure the Phantom Castle is close. -Hmm...

147
00:09:18,753 --> 00:09:21,456
We can't climb this rock wall.

148
00:09:21,990 --> 00:09:24,226
I'll use this chance to take a leak.

149
00:09:24,793 --> 00:09:28,697
Hmm, it's frustrating, but we have no choice but to turn back.

150
00:09:31,133 --> 00:09:32,601
Hmm? Oh?

151
00:09:32,801 --> 00:09:33,802
What happened?

152
00:09:34,002 --> 00:09:35,003
Come here.

153
00:09:35,237 --> 00:09:37,539
Can't you even pee by yourself?

154
00:09:38,140 --> 00:09:41,076
Of course I can! That's not it.

155
00:09:41,276 --> 00:09:42,911
Spill some water here.

156
00:09:43,111 --> 00:09:44,412
Sprinkle some sand on it.

157
00:09:44,613 --> 00:09:46,014
I'm not a cat!

158
00:09:46,848 --> 00:09:48,283
Like this?

159
00:09:54,790 --> 00:09:57,325
You can hear the water flowing.

160
00:09:57,559 --> 00:09:59,928
Hmm, sounds like there's something underneath.

161
00:10:00,929 --> 00:10:03,965
But there's no way we can move a rock this big.

162
00:10:04,332 --> 00:10:06,868
-It moved! -What's this, pumice?

163
00:10:07,469 --> 00:10:09,404
Ryo-san, there is something under it.

164
00:10:10,939 --> 00:10:12,140
Oh!

165
00:10:12,841 --> 00:10:13,675
Yes!

166
00:10:19,848 --> 00:10:21,650
Look, the light of a way out!

167
00:10:28,757 --> 00:10:30,659
Oh! It's a castle!

168
00:10:30,859 --> 00:10:32,961
The Phantom Castle!

169
00:10:35,764 --> 00:10:38,033
We did it! Those are the golden &lt;i&gt;shachihoko&lt;/i&gt;!

170
00:10:40,335 --> 00:10:43,071
We found it! We finally found it!

171
00:10:43,305 --> 00:10:48,043
But normally a castle is built so that it overlooks the world below, right?

172
00:10:48,677 --> 00:10:51,513
This looks more like a hideout.

173
00:10:51,713 --> 00:10:53,215
That's why it's a phantom castle.

174
00:10:53,815 --> 00:10:57,185
The castle lord, a descendant of Lord Shingen, was a recluse.

175
00:10:57,385 --> 00:11:00,722
So he built his castle in this remote area away from the world.

176
00:11:00,922 --> 00:11:05,627
Well, this certainly explains why it hadn't been found until now.

177
00:11:07,495 --> 00:11:10,398
But how can we get those?

178
00:11:10,832 --> 00:11:13,468
There's no bridge around the castle.

179
00:11:13,668 --> 00:11:17,906
This says we enter the castle from the Otemon Gate using &lt;i&gt;hashi&lt;/i&gt; and&lt;i&gt; hashi&lt;/i&gt;.

180
00:11:18,406 --> 00:11:20,208
&lt;i&gt;Hashi&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;hashi&lt;/i&gt;? ("bridge" or "edge" in Japanese)

181
00:11:21,076 --> 00:11:22,944
Hmm? Could it be that?

182
00:11:23,178 --> 00:11:24,946
"BRIDGE"

183
00:11:26,181 --> 00:11:28,216
What? This is too short!

184
00:11:29,050 --> 00:11:30,919
How about using another one?

185
00:11:31,519 --> 00:11:32,754
They're the same length.

186
00:11:32,954 --> 00:11:35,357
Using another one would be the same.

187
00:11:35,590 --> 00:11:36,424
Hmm?

188
00:11:36,658 --> 00:11:38,360
Wait a minute...

189
00:11:38,560 --> 00:11:40,562
Using &lt;i&gt;hashi&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;hashi&lt;/i&gt;...

190
00:11:41,263 --> 00:11:42,197
I got it!

191
00:11:42,831 --> 00:11:44,666
This is how we can cross.

192
00:11:44,866 --> 00:11:45,700
I see.

193
00:11:46,434 --> 00:11:49,871
So it meant using wooden bridges and the edges of the moat.

194
00:11:54,509 --> 00:11:57,279
"DON'T OPEN THIS GATE"

195
00:12:08,156 --> 00:12:09,758
Damn, it really won't open!

196
00:12:09,958 --> 00:12:11,126
It was a sliding door.

197
00:12:12,327 --> 00:12:14,296
What a pointless sign.

198
00:12:15,530 --> 00:12:17,766
Next is a huge iron gate.

199
00:12:21,469 --> 00:12:23,972
No matter how much I push or pull, it won't budge.

200
00:12:24,472 --> 00:12:28,009
The book says that the gate will open when Tatsumi meets Horse.

201
00:12:28,243 --> 00:12:29,110
Is it a code?

202
00:12:29,311 --> 00:12:32,013
So, maybe this statue is the clue.

203
00:12:32,280 --> 00:12:34,582
But something's strange. There's no horse.

204
00:12:34,783 --> 00:12:37,452
I guess Horse is a direction.

205
00:12:37,886 --> 00:12:41,356
In the Edo Period, Horse meant a southerly direction.

206
00:12:41,756 --> 00:12:42,590
That's it!

207
00:12:42,791 --> 00:12:45,493
Turn the Tatsumi statue to the south.

208
00:12:45,727 --> 00:12:47,462
But, what's Tatsumi?

209
00:12:48,296 --> 00:12:51,266
Tatsumi means the dragon and the snake in the Chinese zodiac.

210
00:12:51,466 --> 00:12:53,635
Okay, turn the statue to the south!

211
00:12:53,835 --> 00:12:55,637
Huh? Which way is south?

212
00:12:57,372 --> 00:13:00,608
Hmm, I guess the navigator can't get a signal.

213
00:13:00,809 --> 00:13:01,943
Let's do it another way.

214
00:13:04,112 --> 00:13:05,280
Cutting down a tree?

215
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:06,748
Look at the cut.

216
00:13:07,215 --> 00:13:09,751
The side with the larger growth rings is south.

217
00:13:10,518 --> 00:13:11,353
It's that way.

218
00:13:11,786 --> 00:13:13,521
Turn the dragon to the south.

219
00:13:14,589 --> 00:13:18,026
-And the snake too... -That's not a snake! It's a loach!

220
00:13:24,232 --> 00:13:26,801
Why make such a confusing statue!

221
00:13:27,002 --> 00:13:29,704
Ryo-san, we need to be more careful.

222
00:13:30,472 --> 00:13:33,875
Anyway, the gate's open, so quit complaining.

223
00:13:40,849 --> 00:13:44,886
Huh... so that man has finally come this far.

224
00:13:45,954 --> 00:13:48,390
Seems it's time for me to step in.

225
00:13:49,090 --> 00:13:51,326
For as long as 400 years,

226
00:13:51,860 --> 00:13:55,897
we of the Phantom Clan have guarded this castle without rest.

227
00:13:56,831 --> 00:14:00,201
Lord Shingen, I'm the last of us now.

228
00:14:00,402 --> 00:14:04,005
But don't worry, I won't be bested by the young ones just yet.

229
00:14:04,205 --> 00:14:07,342
I'll show them what we're made of.

230
00:14:31,065 --> 00:14:33,401
This is almost like a haunted house.

231
00:14:33,868 --> 00:14:36,771
That's because it was built hundreds of years ago.

232
00:14:37,305 --> 00:14:40,575
I have no complaints as long as I can get the &lt;i&gt;shachihoko&lt;/i&gt;.

233
00:14:40,942 --> 00:14:43,445
In any case, we need to go up to the top floor.

234
00:14:44,612 --> 00:14:47,282
Ah, if you go that way...

235
00:14:48,950 --> 00:14:50,018
Whoa!

236
00:14:50,552 --> 00:14:53,121
There's a trap ceiling, so you'd better be careful.

237
00:14:53,621 --> 00:14:55,323
Tell me sooner!

238
00:14:57,125 --> 00:14:59,494
The trap is still working.

239
00:15:00,161 --> 00:15:01,896
There could be other traps.

240
00:15:03,098 --> 00:15:04,132
Okay, the second floor.

241
00:15:06,401 --> 00:15:07,635
Ouch, ouch, ouch!

242
00:15:08,503 --> 00:15:11,706
Damn it! This staircase looks like a comedy set.

243
00:15:11,906 --> 00:15:13,608
We can't go any further.

244
00:15:15,877 --> 00:15:17,979
They're in trouble.

245
00:15:18,413 --> 00:15:19,247
Huh?

246
00:15:23,618 --> 00:15:25,253
All right, come up!

247
00:15:26,421 --> 00:15:29,190
This is just the beginning.

248
00:15:33,995 --> 00:15:34,796
What!

249
00:15:36,898 --> 00:15:38,466
"SHORTCUT"

250
00:15:38,666 --> 00:15:39,467
There's more!

251
00:15:43,304 --> 00:15:44,472
How about this!

252
00:15:55,650 --> 00:15:58,453
The traps are getting more serious.

253
00:15:58,653 --> 00:16:01,923
We deserve at least ten golden &lt;i&gt;shachihoko&lt;/i&gt; for this.

254
00:16:02,323 --> 00:16:04,692
Greedy fools...

255
00:16:05,660 --> 00:16:07,529
Well then, time for my next move.

256
00:16:09,797 --> 00:16:11,799
Finally, the third floor.

257
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:15,670
The top floor is the fifth, so we're only halfway.

258
00:16:16,004 --> 00:16:18,406
Anyway, let's find the stairs.

259
00:16:19,374 --> 00:16:20,208
Oh?

260
00:16:20,875 --> 00:16:22,143
What's that?

261
00:16:22,343 --> 00:16:23,478
There's some writing.

262
00:16:24,245 --> 00:16:26,381
"To the top floor of the tower"?

263
00:16:26,948 --> 00:16:30,718
Oh, could it be an elevator?

264
00:16:31,152 --> 00:16:33,688
Hey, isn't this another trap?

265
00:16:33,888 --> 00:16:36,124
Oh! There's an old gold coin here!

266
00:16:36,324 --> 00:16:37,492
What?

267
00:16:38,126 --> 00:16:40,495
Turns out it's just a brass plate.

268
00:16:42,530 --> 00:16:43,731
"DIRECT TO HELL"

269
00:16:44,032 --> 00:16:44,999
Oh no!

270
00:16:48,203 --> 00:16:49,737
It won't open!

271
00:16:50,271 --> 00:16:51,406
Who's there?

272
00:16:52,540 --> 00:16:56,210
I thought you had some backbone, but you're still green.

273
00:16:59,180 --> 00:17:01,983
Oh! You're that dodgy old man from the teahouse!

274
00:17:02,283 --> 00:17:04,385
Who are you calling a dodgy old man?

275
00:17:04,586 --> 00:17:07,188
I won't be insulted by a fool blinded by greed!

276
00:17:07,388 --> 00:17:09,290
Just get us out of here!

277
00:17:09,891 --> 00:17:14,062
You entered this castle guarded by the Phantom Clan without permission.

278
00:17:14,262 --> 00:17:16,464
I cannot let you out of there.

279
00:17:17,298 --> 00:17:18,600
The Random Clan?

280
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:20,535
The Phantom Clan!

281
00:17:20,902 --> 00:17:24,372
Hmph, you came here to get the golden &lt;i&gt;shachihoko&lt;/i&gt;, right?

282
00:17:24,572 --> 00:17:28,643
But as long as I'm here, you won't even lay a finger on them.

283
00:17:29,210 --> 00:17:33,081
Oh really? I'll not only touch them, but rub my cheek against them.

284
00:17:33,648 --> 00:17:35,650
Oh, you're very confident.

285
00:17:35,883 --> 00:17:40,421
Very well. If you manage to touch them, I'll allow you to have them.

286
00:17:40,622 --> 00:17:43,658
But you'll have to get out of there first.

287
00:17:45,727 --> 00:17:46,761
Damn it!

288
00:17:46,961 --> 00:17:49,464
All right, don't forget what you just said!

289
00:17:49,664 --> 00:17:52,333
For a billion yen, this is nothing!

290
00:17:54,302 --> 00:17:55,670
He's a monster.

291
00:17:57,505 --> 00:17:58,740
-Well then... -Huh?

292
00:17:59,774 --> 00:18:00,808
Farewell!

293
00:18:08,783 --> 00:18:12,420
Oh, jeez, we're back to square one again.

294
00:18:13,888 --> 00:18:15,957
Ryo-san, let's give up now.

295
00:18:16,157 --> 00:18:18,793
I'll never give up!

296
00:18:18,993 --> 00:18:22,163
That old man said he'd give them to us if I touched them.

297
00:18:22,363 --> 00:18:26,501
And I'll gladly take those billion-yen &lt;i&gt;shachihoko&lt;/i&gt;!

298
00:18:33,107 --> 00:18:34,142
Here goes!

299
00:18:36,644 --> 00:18:38,379
Amazing!

300
00:18:38,713 --> 00:18:41,149
I can't believe you could reach that far.

301
00:18:41,349 --> 00:18:42,650
Nothing is impossible for me!

302
00:18:43,251 --> 00:18:45,787
He might be in the Phantom Clan or whatever,

303
00:18:45,987 --> 00:18:49,524
but if he blocks the inside, I'll just climb the outside.

304
00:18:49,724 --> 00:18:52,260
I should've done this from the start.

305
00:18:53,628 --> 00:18:55,830
Hey, Ryo-san!

306
00:18:56,030 --> 00:18:57,799
Be careful!

307
00:18:59,834 --> 00:19:02,136
Okay, I'm almost there.

308
00:19:04,572 --> 00:19:07,709
I'll praise you for making it this far.

309
00:19:08,176 --> 00:19:11,379
Huh! You again. You stubborn old man!

310
00:19:12,513 --> 00:19:16,184
Playtime is over. I can't let you leave.

311
00:19:16,384 --> 00:19:18,519
What? I can't pull out my sword.

312
00:19:18,720 --> 00:19:21,522
My body... has become stiff?

313
00:19:21,723 --> 00:19:24,225
-I can't deal with this. -Hey, wait!

314
00:19:24,425 --> 00:19:26,227
All right, now's my chance!

315
00:19:27,962 --> 00:19:28,996
It's hot!

316
00:19:29,697 --> 00:19:31,833
Ninja Arts, Fire Style!

317
00:19:32,533 --> 00:19:33,601
This ends now!

318
00:19:34,535 --> 00:19:39,774
DON'T TRY THIS AT HOME, KIDS!

319
00:19:41,008 --> 00:19:42,577
Don't prepare it in front of me.

320
00:19:46,581 --> 00:19:47,849
Damn it! Huh?

321
00:19:48,049 --> 00:19:51,586
The way he moves, he's no ordinary guy.

322
00:19:51,786 --> 00:19:53,721
He must be an Uesugi ninja!

323
00:19:55,723 --> 00:19:56,557
I did it!

324
00:19:57,325 --> 00:19:59,160
My golden &lt;i&gt;shachihoko&lt;/i&gt;-chan!

325
00:19:59,360 --> 00:20:01,062
Stop!

326
00:20:03,631 --> 00:20:05,767
Don't touch that &lt;i&gt;shachihoko&lt;/i&gt;.

327
00:20:06,267 --> 00:20:09,337
Come on! You promised to give them to us if I touched them.

328
00:20:10,538 --> 00:20:12,340
Just don't touch it!

329
00:20:12,774 --> 00:20:16,177
Shut up! It's mine and I'll do what I want!

330
00:20:17,178 --> 00:20:19,247
Stop! I told you not to touch it!

331
00:20:21,048 --> 00:20:23,084
-Heh, got it! -Ah!

332
00:20:23,384 --> 00:20:25,887
Oh no... It's too late.

333
00:20:30,258 --> 00:20:31,559
It's over.

334
00:20:31,926 --> 00:20:33,928
I understand your frustration,

335
00:20:34,128 --> 00:20:38,266
but you have a nice castle even without the &lt;i&gt;shachihoko&lt;/i&gt;, don't you?

336
00:20:38,466 --> 00:20:39,567
What's that?

337
00:20:40,067 --> 00:20:43,905
If the &lt;i&gt;shachihoko&lt;/i&gt; are taken, the whole castle will collapse.

338
00:20:44,305 --> 00:20:45,373
What?

339
00:20:45,773 --> 00:20:51,746
That way, Lord Shingen's golden &lt;i&gt;shachihoko&lt;/i&gt; will never fall into anyone else's hands.

340
00:20:52,280 --> 00:20:54,615
What on earth is going on?

341
00:20:58,085 --> 00:21:01,422
At this point, no one can stop it.

342
00:21:01,622 --> 00:21:05,927
I'll give the golden &lt;i&gt;shachihoko&lt;/i&gt; to you as I promised.

343
00:21:06,861 --> 00:21:08,095
Oh! W-What's that?

344
00:21:24,478 --> 00:21:26,948
Old man, we're in trouble. Let's get out of here.

345
00:21:27,415 --> 00:21:29,884
I shall go down with the castle.

346
00:21:30,117 --> 00:21:31,619
Don't be foolish!

347
00:21:31,819 --> 00:21:34,155
You had potential.

348
00:21:34,689 --> 00:21:35,523
Farewell.

349
00:21:36,090 --> 00:21:37,725
Hey! Hey!

350
00:21:38,559 --> 00:21:39,660
Oops!

351
00:21:45,566 --> 00:21:46,634
Damn!

352
00:22:00,915 --> 00:22:04,585
It's really turned into a phantom now.

353
00:22:04,819 --> 00:22:07,188
No one will ever believe us.

354
00:22:08,923 --> 00:22:10,691
No worries, we have these.

355
00:22:14,896 --> 00:22:16,197
"KAMEARI PARK POLICE STATION"

356
00:22:16,397 --> 00:22:18,132
Well, impressed?

357
00:22:18,833 --> 00:22:21,402
This whole thing is mine.

358
00:22:22,003 --> 00:22:24,505
Feast your eyes, everyone.

359
00:22:25,172 --> 00:22:26,541
Especially you, Chief.

360
00:22:26,741 --> 00:22:29,744
Living an honest life, you'd never see this in your lifetime.

361
00:22:29,944 --> 00:22:34,548
Hmph! It must be some gold-plated fake from a souvenir shop.

362
00:22:34,749 --> 00:22:38,252
Ah, a typical poor person.

363
00:22:38,519 --> 00:22:42,056
Look at this shine, this brilliance.

364
00:22:42,256 --> 00:22:44,692
How could this possibly be a gold-plated fake?

365
00:22:46,060 --> 00:22:48,629
Oh no! I must've bumped it around too much.

366
00:22:49,196 --> 00:22:52,333
Oh dear, the base metal is showing, Ryo-chan.

367
00:22:52,533 --> 00:22:54,168
What's this?

368
00:22:54,368 --> 00:22:57,338
I-It really is gold-plated!

369
00:22:58,372 --> 00:23:00,975
And judging from that tacky shine,

370
00:23:01,208 --> 00:23:04,178
it seems the plating itself isn't worth much either.

371
00:23:04,779 --> 00:23:07,915
That &lt;i&gt;shachihoko&lt;/i&gt; is just like you.

372
00:23:09,083 --> 00:23:11,519
Damn that old man!

373
00:23:19,293 --> 00:23:21,062
Ah! Stop it!

374
00:23:21,262 --> 00:23:23,464
This old man is so naughty!

375
00:23:23,664 --> 00:23:26,267
I'm no old man.

376
00:23:26,467 --> 00:23:28,469
Call me "uncle" instead.

377
00:23:28,936 --> 00:23:31,639
Hmm, actually, "big brother" sounds better.

378
00:23:31,839 --> 00:23:34,475
Ehh, we can't do that.

379
00:23:34,675 --> 00:23:36,644
Yeah, you're too old to be our big brother.

380
00:23:36,978 --> 00:23:38,980
Oh? Is that so?

381
00:23:39,213 --> 00:23:41,849
Then, I suppose I'll be keeping this to myself.

382
00:23:44,151 --> 00:23:46,554
Oh! Big brother!

383
00:23:46,854 --> 00:23:49,323
The castle's gone, and I'm finally free.

384
00:23:49,557 --> 00:23:52,259
Now I can enjoy the rest of my life.

385
00:23:54,562 --> 00:23:56,964
Here, here, you want this?

386
00:23:57,164 --> 00:23:59,033
I want it!
